  "title": "Balancing Redox Equations in Basic Solutions",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Recall that basic solutions have excess hydroxide ions. Some of these hydroxide ions react with hydrogen ions to produce water. The simplest way to generate the balanced overall equation in basic solution is to start with the balanced equation in acidic solution, then convert it to the equation for basic solution."
              }
            ],
            "id": "hlnx57bhizye6qt",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "ywq0g6ivuc3d47z",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "5h3kgrbkw1qbknu",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/A3/A31F9808B584CB71B1FEA56DD0BCDE4E/green_line.png",
            "type": "img"
